@startuml
title Governed legal workflow -> focused DASHI TOE

skinparam componentStyle rectangle

package "Canonical theorem owners" {
  [SensibLaw operational / review / matter]
  [Legal source authority / applicability]
  [Compositional compliance]
  [ITIR governance controls]
  [Semantic promotion / acquisition]
  [Formalisation / external-world boundary]
}

component "GovernedLegalWorkflowTOEBridgeExact" as Bridge
component "EverythingTOESymmetryResolved369" as TOE
component "DASHI.Unifier" as Unifier
component "DASHI.Unified.Everything" as Unified

[SensibLaw operational / review / matter] --> Bridge : exact reuse
[Legal source authority / applicability] --> Bridge : exact reuse
[Compositional compliance] --> Bridge : witness-preserving composition
[ITIR governance controls] --> Bridge : controls are not certification
[Semantic promotion / acquisition] --> Bridge : non-promotion
[Formalisation / external-world boundary] --> Bridge : proof is not world truth

Bridge --> TOE : direct fail-closed aliases
Bridge --> Unifier : direct fail-closed aliases
Bridge --> Unified : direct fail-closed aliases

note right of Bridge
O: normalize existing governance proofs
R: reuse canonical owners
C: aliases only
S: workflow state cannot promote truth or authority
L: one governance normalization lane
P: preserve intermediate compliance witness
G: standards are lenses, not certification
F: referee/preflight/kernel checks remain separate receipts
end note

note bottom of TOE
No Actionstep-specific ontology is introduced.
Matter/task/workflow product state is consumed
through the existing generic legal-workflow owners.
end note
@enduml
